    "created_at": "2025-07-11T03:37:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-07-11T03:37:25Z",
    "body": "Thanks for the ping.\n\nLooking at the history of this behavior, it seems to have been introduced in the following Mozilla bug, which was implemented by @saschanaz: [Bug 1738905 - Disable bfcache when active lock/request exists in SharedWorker](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1738905).\n\nAs @fergald pointed out, it seems that allowing the page into BFCache might be safe, since the SharedWorker can still release the lock, for example, through a message from another active document.\n\nI am curious about the original rationale for preventing pages holding a WebLock from entering BFCache. Could you elaborate on the specific use cases or edge cases that were a concern and led to this implementation?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
