    "created_at": "2025-07-11T15:26:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-07-11T15:26:16Z",
    "body": "@smaug---- probably is the most important Gecko feedback-provider, but from a workers perspective I agree that this constraint can be relaxed.\n\nI think the conceptual ideal for Web Lock interaction with SharedWorkers would be that if running code attempts to acquire a lock that is held by a SharedWorker that is frozen because all of its connected documents are in BFCache, then the SharedWorker should potentially be terminated and cause its connected documents to be removed from BFCache and the SharedWorker.  (Although if https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11205 introduces restartable SharedWorkers then the ShW could just be terminated.)  I'm not saying we specify that (at this moment), just that we should have a good (documented) reason if we impose a more restrictive constraint than that.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
